{
  "title": { "en": "Sorting machine" },
  "optional": true,
  "tray": "pipeline",
  "after": {
    "en": "This sorting machine combines local features into a class decision: convolutions can find different strokes, nonlinearities and pooling help with changes in position, and the classifier scores each class from the features. Passing on these new parts shows it works beyond the training examples; assessing reliability in practice requires more representative tests."
  },
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "The sorter goes live: parts sit in different places, at different strengths, some with noise. The last few sets are \"new parts\" that take no part in training and are only checked."
      },
      "fig": { "test": 0, "caption": { "en": "Set 1: an X" } }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "From image to class, a network first extracts local features and then combines them into class scores. AlexNet combined convolution, activation, pooling and classification layers and trained on many images; this level is a much smaller classification example."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "For a new set of parts, we do not always have to start from scratch: we can reuse a trained feature extractor and train only a new classification head. If the old features do not fit well enough, we can unfreeze some layers and train them further; this is fine-tuning. This level still trains on its current task."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "Use the Softmax part unlocked in <level-ref to=\"4-18\"></level-ref> to turn three scores into probabilities, or build the conversion yourself."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "Your task in this level: output three probabilities, above 0.55 for the right class and below 0.45 for the other two. Something to think about: which strokes tell the three kinds apart? How many kinds of stroke must the network see?"
      }
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "4-21",
      "kind": "graph",
      "brief": {
        "en": "The parts on the belt come in three kinds, X, O and +, at different places and strengths, some with noise. Output three probabilities: above 0.55 for the right class, below 0.45 for the other two. The \"new parts\" at the end of the list take no part in training and are only checked."
      },
      "hint": {
        "en": "One convolution channel can pick out only one kind of stroke; how many do three classes need at least? Each class's score can take a share from every channel's feature. Once built, train for a while and watch the two error lines."
      },
      "outputs": ["px", "po", "pp"],
      "outputLabels": { "px": { "en": "Is X" }, "po": { "en": "Is O" }, "pp": { "en": "Is +" } },
      "check": { "tolerance": 0.45 },
      "trainRate": 80,
      "scene": "sorter",
      "tests": [
        { "label": { "en": "X 1" }, "part": "X", "ox": 1, "oy": 2, "ink": 0.75, "seed": 0 },
